    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d255">

                <pb facs="0248" n="926" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg926"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 30.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-03-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 3, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch No. 31, of the 12th of
                    December last, was, with its accompaniments, received at this department on
                    Sunday, the 1st instant, <hi rendition="#italic">via</hi> St. Petersburgh. Your
                    proceedings to which it relates are approved.</p>
                <pb facs="0249" n="927" xml:id="pg927"/>
                <p>With reference to the objections of the Chinese authorities to our consuls being
                    engaged in trade, I have to observe that this is a subject requiring the
                    legislative action of Congress, which, being on the eve of adjournment when the
                    question arises, it must be deferred until next session, when it will be laid
                    before that body.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anson Burlingame</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
